<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov industrial output down prelim 1.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov industrial output down prelim 1.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production fell a preliminary 1.9 percent in November from the previous month on a seasonally adjusted basis, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of the preliminary monthly figures follows: Seasonally adjusted month-on-month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>				  NOV     MONTH AGO     NOV INDEX</p>
<p> Output			 -1.9	+3.9	  99.6</p>
<p> Shipments		    -0.8	+3.7	 102.2</p>
<p> Inventories		  -0.9	+0.7	 107.4</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	 +1.3	-4.0	 112.7</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year (in pct):</p>
<p>				   NOV     MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output			  +4.0	+6.5</p>
<p> Shipments		     +5.1	+6.8</p>
<p> Inventories		   -0.7	-0.1</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	 -4.1	-5.7</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of MITI's forecasts for manufacturers' output:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted, month-on-month (in pct):</p>
<p>		     DEC forecast   JAN forecast</p>
<p>		     +0.8	     +5.1</p>
<p>MITI said in a statement that Japan's industrial output was on a gradual recovery track.</p>
</text>
